From 0caa1a52391e2459441d6f4e4923ac765d2dfab6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:11:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/23] can: isotp: check the CAN FD tx_flags in
 CAN_ISOTP_LL_OPTS

The tx_flags of struct can_isotp_ll_options are set into the flags of
the created CAN FD frames. For CAN CC they have to be zero but for CAN
FD any value was accepted and copied into the CAN FD frames, including
CANFD_ESI and undefined flags.

For the ISO-TP transmission only the bit rate switch (CANFD_BRS) is a
relevant property of the CAN FD frames. The error state indicator
(CANFD_ESI) reflects the error state of the transmitting CAN controller
and is no transmission parameter of the ISO-TP protocol.

This is an intentional tightening of the uAPI and no bug fix: accept
CANFD_BRS and the CANFD_FDF marker (which is set by the CAN core anyway)
and reject other tx_flags with -EINVAL. CAN FD frames with CANFD_ESI
can still be sent with CAN_RAW sockets, e.g. for testing purposes.

The CAN core sets the CANFD_FDF marker in the CAN FD frames when they
are sent. Add CANFD_FDF to the stored tx_flags for CAN FD already in
setsockopt(), so that getsockopt() returns the flags of the created CAN
FD frames. The CAN frames on the bus are not changed by this.

Document the accepted tx_flags in isotp.h and iso15765-2.rst.

Signed-off-by: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
---
 Documentation/networking/iso15765-2.rst | 6 +++++-
 include/uapi/linux/can/isotp.h          | 2 ++
 net/can/isotp.c                         | 9 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/networking/iso15765-2.rst b/Documentation/networking/iso15765-2.rst
index 1962209..1cbe488 100644
--- a/Documentation/networking/iso15765-2.rst
+++ b/Documentation/networking/iso15765-2.rst
@@ -287,7 +287,11 @@ where the ``can_isotp_ll_options`` structure has the following contents:
   traffic (i.e.: ``mtu = CANFD_MTU``).
 
 * ``tx_flags``: flags set into ``struct canfd_frame.flags`` at frame creation.
-  Only applies to CAN FD traffic (i.e.: ``mtu = CANFD_MTU``).
+  Only applies to CAN FD traffic (i.e.: ``mtu = CANFD_MTU``) and has to be
+  ``0`` for classical CAN frames. Only the ``CANFD_BRS`` flag (and the
+  ``CANFD_FDF`` marker) can be set, other flags are rejected with ``-EINVAL``.
+  The ``CANFD_FDF`` marker is always added for CAN FD traffic, so that
+  ``getsockopt()`` returns the flags of the created CAN FD frames.
 
 Transmission stmin
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/can/isotp.h b/include/uapi/linux/can/isotp.h
index a2e5aa6..eb8b529 100644
--- a/include/uapi/linux/can/isotp.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/can/isotp.h
@@ -119,6 +119,8 @@ struct can_isotp_ll_options {
 
 	__u8  tx_flags;		/* set into struct canfd_frame.flags	*/
 				/* at frame creation: e.g. CANFD_BRS	*/
+				/* only CANFD_BRS and CANFD_FDF allowed */
+				/* CANFD_FDF is always set for CAN FD	*/
 				/* Obsolete when the BRS flag is fixed	*/
 				/* by the CAN netdriver configuration	*/
 };
diff --git a/net/can/isotp.c b/net/can/isotp.c
index ce541e5..ea3790a 100644
--- a/net/can/isotp.c
+++ b/net/can/isotp.c
@@ -1796,8 +1796,17 @@ static int isotp_setsockopt_locked(struct socket *sock, int optname,
 		    (ll->tx_dl > CAN_MAX_DLEN || ll->tx_flags != 0))
 			return -EINVAL;
 
+		/* only CANFD_BRS (and the CANFD_FDF marker) for CAN FD frames */
+		if (ll->mtu == CANFD_MTU &&
+		    (ll->tx_flags & ~(CANFD_BRS | CANFD_FDF)))
+			return -EINVAL;
+
 		memcpy(&so->ll, ll, sizeof(*ll));
 
+		/* CAN FD frames are always marked with CANFD_FDF */
+		if (so->ll.mtu == CANFD_MTU)
+			so->ll.tx_flags |= CANFD_FDF;
+
 		/* set ll_dl for tx path to similar place as for rx */
 		so->tx.ll_dl = ll->tx_dl;
 		break;
